<title>JAPAN: Japan May soybean crushing up 7.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan May soybean crushing up 7.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's soybean crushing in May reached 318,628 tonnes, up 7.8 percent from a year earlier, and rapeseed crushing was 178,766 tonnes, up 11.5 percent from May 1996, Agriculture Ministry data showed.</p>
<p>The country's output of soy oil during May was 57,089 tonnes and that of soymeal 242,116 tonnes, it showed.</p>
<p>The following are details of the ministry's imported</p>
<p>oilseeds crushing and stock data (in tonnes):</p>
<p> -- Soybeans -- May 97	 May 96     Jan-May 97   Jan-May 96</p>
<p> Crushing	318,628	295,699     1,538,684    1,512,705</p>
<p> Oil output     57,089	 53,647	 275,748	272,447</p>
<p> Meal output   242,116	227,863     1,174,467    1,168,642</p>
<p>-- Rapeseed --</p>
<p> Crushing	178,766	160,299	 818,995	799,983</p>
<p> Oil output     75,440	 68,308	 344,194	340,706</p>
<p> Meal output   101,208	 90,892	 459,455	451,595</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
